msgstr "Жемчужный глаз"

#. ja: アバラシアビターリング
#. de: abalathisch[a] Bitterling
#. fr: bouvière d'Abalathia
#. column 2: Abalathian bitterlings
#. column 8: The Abalathian bitterling's ivory white skin easily distinguishes it from its silver cousins also found in the freshwater rivers and lakes of Gyr Abania.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
#. column 9: Abalathian Bitterling
msgctxt "Item:20042:0:0"
msgid "Abalathian bitterling"
msgstr "абалатийский горчак"

#. de: abalathisch[a] Bitterlinge
#. fr: bouvières d'Abalathia
#. column 0: Abalathian bitterling
#. column 8: The Abalathian bitterling's ivory white skin easily distinguishes it from its silver cousins also found in the freshwater rivers and lakes of Gyr Abania.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
#. column 9: Abalathian Bitterling
msgctxt "Item:20042:0:2"
msgid "Abalathian bitterlings"
msgstr "абалатийские горчаки"

#. ja: 真っ白な魚体が特徴的な淡水魚<br>[魚拓額縁G1に設定可能]
#. de: Durch die elfenbeinweiße Haut des abalathischen Bitterlings ist er leicht von seinen silbernen Artgenossen zu unterscheiden, die ebenfalls in den Flüssen und Seen von Gyr Abania heimisch sind. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe S ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: La peau blanche ivoirée de la bouvière d'Abalathia permet de la distinguer facilement de ses cousins argentés qui vivent dans les rivières d'eau douce et les lacs de Gyr Abania.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de petite taille]
#. column 0: Abalathian bitterling
#. column 2: Abalathian bitterlings
#. column 9: Abalathian Bitterling
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:20042:0:8"
msgid "The Abalathian bitterling's ivory white skin easily distinguishes it from its silver cousins also found in the freshwater rivers and lakes of Gyr Abania.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]"
msgstr "Абалатийского горчака легко отличить от его серебристых сородичей, которые тоже водятся в пресных реках и озёрах Гир Абании: кожа у него цвета слоновой кости.<br><br>[Можно поместить в малую рыбную раму.]"

#. ja: アバラシアビターリング
#. de: Abalathischer Bitterling
#. fr: Bouvière d'Abalathia
#. column 0: Abalathian bitterling
#. column 2: Abalathian bitterlings
#. column 8: The Abalathian bitterling's ivory white skin easily distinguishes it from its silver cousins also found in the freshwater rivers and lakes of Gyr Abania.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:20042:0:9"
msgid "Abalathian Bitterling"
msgstr "Абалатийский горчак"

#. ja: スティールシャーク
#. de: Stahlhai
#. fr: requin-acier
#. column 2: steelsharks
#. column 8: One of only a few freshwater sharks discovered in Eorzea, the steelshark can primarily be found in the rivers and lakes of Gyr Abania.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
#. column 9: Steelshark
msgctxt "Item:20043:0:0"
msgid "steelshark"
msgstr "стальная акула"

